"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Equivalent; dead code"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"markPendingLocalChanges"},{"type":"text","value":" covered a handler that syncs before its transaction is registered. Since #1986, each direct path registers the transaction and recomputes, which rebuilds "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"pendingLocalChanges"},{"type":"text","value":", before "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"commit()"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"S5, S6, S12"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Equivalent; dead code"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The truncate reapply search for an earlier insert never finds one (round-1 A2 to A4)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"S7, M10"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Equivalent"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recompute's stale cleanup removes the leftover layer; "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isPersisted"},{"type":"text","value":" awaiters resume after the synchronous state change"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"S2"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Equivalent on reached histories"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The completed-key fallback decides 219 times, all in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"collection-metadata-publication-oracle"},{"type":"text","value":", which asserts the exact published batches and passes. Another publication delivers the settlement update"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"C1, C2"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Equivalent on reached histories"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Batch composition ran 228 times in the suite; insert-first pairs never ran, including in a targeted history"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"C3"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Minor"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A composed delete keeps a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"previousValue"},{"type":"text","value":" beside the correct "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"value"},{"type":"text","value":"; reached once"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"witness","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Witness"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The same-key lane of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"optimistic-transaction-oracle.property.test.ts"},{"type":"text","value":" adds\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"delete-insert"},{"type":"text","value":". The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"applyMutations"},{"type":"text","value":" truth table gives its net request: a\nreinsert that restores the original row cancels the pair; otherwise it is an\nupdate from the original row whose "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"changes"},{"type":"text","value":" hold exactly the differing\nfields. The lane checks both authored prefixes, so the reinserted row must be\nvisible optimistically. Two pinned cases cover a restoring reinsert, which\ngeneration never produces."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Mutant on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"transactions.ts"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Owner result"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"M8: the merged update loses "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"optimistic"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3 of 66 fail"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"X1: the reinsert is passed through as an insert"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"13 of 66 fail"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"X2: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"changes"},{"type":"text","value":" hold the whole reinserted row"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"12 of 66 fail"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"X3: a restoring reinsert is not canceled"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"4 of 68 fail, including both pinned cases"}]}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"open","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Open"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The completed-key fallback (S2) and the insert-first batch compositions\n(C1, C2) may be unreachable. Proving that would let the state-stack port\ndelete them."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The port can delete "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"markPendingLocalChanges"},{"type":"text","value":", the truncate reapply search,\nand the recompute delete filter."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"verification","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Verification"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"packages/db"},{"type":"text","value":" Vitest, typecheck off: 201 files, 7,865 tests."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"state-mutation-round-2","text":"State mutation round 2","level":1},{"id":"round","text":"Round","level":2},{"id":"witness","text":"Witness","level":2},{"id":"open","text":"Open","level":2},{"id":"verification","text":"Verification","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"# State mutation round 2\n\nReviewed executable revision: `76484a092`, the test commit that precedes\nthis record (base `4ce1f9b87`). No production code changes.\n\n## Round\n\nAfter the round-1 fixes merged (#1986, #1995, #1996), 40 new source mutants\nmodeled plausible mistakes in the state.ts sync commit (12), change batching\nand subscription delivery (14), and mutations.ts and transactions.ts (14).\nEach was applied to unchanged `main`; the full db suite ran with bail. The\nround-1 survivors were rerun first: every round-1 test gap is now caught.\n\n28 of the 40 were caught. Each of the 12 survivors was classified:\n\n| Mutants | Verdict | Evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| M8 | **Test gap**, closed here | A delete then a reinsert of the same key in one transaction, merged as an update, lost its optimistic flag. The row showed its old value until persistence. The same-key lane never authored a delete followed by an insert |\n| M1, M2, M3 | Equivalent; dead code | `markPendingLocalChanges` covered a handler that syncs before its transaction is registered. Since #1986, each direct path registers the transaction and recomputes, which rebuilds `pendingLocalChanges`, before `commit()` |\n| S5, S6, S12 | Equivalent; dead code | The truncate reapply search for an earlier insert never finds one (round-1 A2 to A4) |\n| S7, M10 | Equivalent | Recompute's stale cleanup removes the leftover layer; `isPersisted` awaiters resume after the synchronous state change |\n| S2 | Equivalent on reached histories | The completed-key fallback decides 219 times, all in `collection-metadata-publication-oracle`, which asserts the exact published batches and passes. Another publication delivers the settlement update |\n| C1, C2 | Equivalent on reached histories | Batch composition ran 228 times in the suite; insert-first pairs never ran, including in a targeted history |\n| C3 | Minor | A composed delete keeps a `previousValue` beside the correct `value`; reached once |\n\n## Witness\n\nThe same-key lane of `optimistic-transaction-oracle.property.test.ts` adds\n`delete-insert`. The `applyMutations` truth table gives its net request: a\nreinsert that restores the original row cancels the pair; otherwise it is an\nupdate from the original row whose `changes` hold exactly the differing\nfields. The lane checks both authored prefixes, so the reinserted row must be\nvisible optimistically. Two pinned cases cover a restoring reinsert, which\ngeneration never produces.\n\n| Mutant on `transactions.ts` | Owner result |\n| --- | --- |\n| M8: the merged update loses `optimistic` | 3 of 66 fail |\n| X1: the reinsert is passed through as an insert | 13 of 66 fail |\n| X2: `changes` hold the whole reinserted row | 12 of 66 fail |\n| X3: a restoring reinsert is not canceled | 4 of 68 fail, including both pinned cases |\n\n## Open\n\n- The completed-key fallback (S2) and the insert-first batch compositions\n  (C1, C2) may be unreachable. Proving that would let the state-stack port\n  delete them.\n- The port can delete `markPendingLocalChanges`, the truncate reapply search,\n  and the recompute delete filter.\n\n## Verification\n\n`packages/db` Vitest, typecheck off: 201 files, 7,865 tests.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"# State mutation round 2\n\nReviewed executable revision: `76484a092`, the test commit that precedes\nthis record (base `4ce1f9b87`). No production code changes.\n\n## Round\n\nAfter the round-1 fixes merged (#1986, #1995, #1996), 40 new source mutants\nmodeled plausible mistakes in the state.ts sync commit (12), change batching\nand subscription delivery (14), and mutations.ts and transactions.ts (14).\nEach was applied to unchanged `main`; the full db suite ran with bail. The\nround-1 survivors were rerun first: every round-1 test gap is now caught.\n\n28 of the 40 were caught. Each of the 12 survivors was classified:\n\n| Mutants | Verdict | Evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| M8 | **Test gap**, closed here | A delete then a reinsert of the same key in one transaction, merged as an update, lost its optimistic flag. The row showed its old value until persistence. The same-key lane never authored a delete followed by an insert |\n| M1, M2, M3 | Equivalent; dead code | `markPendingLocalChanges` covered a handler that syncs before its transaction is registered. Since #1986, each direct path registers the transaction and recomputes, which rebuilds `pendingLocalChanges`, before `commit()` |\n| S5, S6, S12 | Equivalent; dead code | The truncate reapply search for an earlier insert never finds one (round-1 A2 to A4) |\n| S7, M10 | Equivalent | Recompute's stale cleanup removes the leftover layer; `isPersisted` awaiters resume after the synchronous state change |\n| S2 | Equivalent on reached histories | The completed-key fallback decides 219 times, all in `collection-metadata-publication-oracle`, which asserts the exact published batches and passes. Another publication delivers the settlement update |\n| C1, C2 | Equivalent on reached histories | Batch composition ran 228 times in the suite; insert-first pairs never ran, including in a targeted history |\n| C3 | Minor | A composed delete keeps a `previousValue` beside the correct `value`; reached once |\n\n## Witness\n\nThe same-key lane of `optimistic-transaction-oracle.property.test.ts` adds\n`delete-insert`. The `applyMutations` truth table gives its net request: a\nreinsert that restores the original row cancels the pair; otherwise it is an\nupdate from the original row whose `changes` hold exactly the differing\nfields. The lane checks both authored prefixes, so the reinserted row must be\nvisible optimistically. Two pinned cases cover a restoring reinsert, which\ngeneration never produces.\n\n| Mutant on `transactions.ts` | Owner result |\n| --- | --- |\n| M8: the merged update loses `optimistic` | 3 of 66 fail |\n| X1: the reinsert is passed through as an insert | 13 of 66 fail |\n| X2: `changes` hold the whole reinserted row | 12 of 66 fail |\n| X3: a restoring reinsert is not canceled | 4 of 68 fail, including both pinned cases |\n\n## Open\n\n- The completed-key fallback (S2) and the insert-first batch compositions\n  (C1, C2) may be unreachable. Proving that would let the state-stack port\n  delete them.\n- The port can delete `markPendingLocalChanges`, the truncate reapply search,\n  and the recompute delete filter.\n\n## Verification\n\n`packages/db` Vitest, typecheck off: 201 files, 7,865 tests.\n"}
